Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "HGNC_gene_symbol" (RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION_UNC_RSEM): filter to the TP53 gene.  
• "normalized_count" (RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION_UNC_RSEM): raw expression value that will be log10‑transformed.  
• "project_short_name" (both tables): restrict to the TCGA‑BRCA cohort.  
• "sample_barcode" (RNASEQ_GENE_EXPRESSION_UNC_RSEM): primary key for expression samples.  
• "Hugo_Symbol" (SOMATIC_MUTATION_MC3): restrict to TP53 in mutation data.  
• "Variant_Classification" (SOMATIC_MUTATION_MC3): treat as the “mutation type” grouping variable.  
• "sample_barcode_tumor" (SOMATIC_MUTATION_MC3): sample identifier that must be aligned (substring) with "sample_barcode" from expression data.  
Typical filter conditions  
• "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
• "HGNC_gene_symbol" ILIKE '%TP53%' (expression)  
• "Hugo_Symbol"  = 'TP53'          (mutation)  
• "normalized_count" > 0           (to allow LOG10 transform)  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL queries — from simple look‑ups to the full one‑way ANOVA calculation.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes and every exploratory query is capped with `LIMIT 20`.

```sql
