Table full name: TCGA_HG19_DATA_V0.TCGA_HG19_DATA_V0.SOMATIC_MUTATION_DCC
Column name: Validation_Method Type: TEXT Description: The assay platforms used for the validation call
Column name: HGNC_UniProt_ID_Supplied_By_UniProt Type: TEXT Description: UniProt ID
Column name: HGNC_Locus_Group Type: TEXT Description: HGNC Locus Group
Column name: Normal_Validation_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Matched normal genotyping (validation) for allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases (cleared in somatic MAF)
Column name: Protein_Change Type: TEXT Description: Changes an amino acid to another amino acid e.g. p.G464V
Column name: COSMIC_Total_Alterations_In_Gene Type: NUMBER Description: Total Alteration in Gene
Column name: GO_Cellular_Component Type: TEXT Description: GO Cellular Component. For more information: http://geneontology.org/docs/ontology-documentation/
Column name: OREGANNO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Open Regulatory Annotation Database Id. Example: OREG0026204, OREG0023259
Column name: Ref_Context Type: TEXT Description: Reference allele per VCF specs, and its five flanking base pairs
Column name: sample_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: Variant_Classification Type: TEXT Description: Translational effect of variant allele
Column name: UniProt_Region Type: TEXT Description: UniProt Region
Column name: Normal_Validation_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Matched normal genotyping (validation) for allele 2 (cleared in somatic MAF)
Column name: Entrez_Gene_Id Type: NUMBER Description: Entrez gene ID (an integer). 0 is used for regions that do not correspond to a gene region or Ensembl ID
Column name: GENCODE_Transcript_Name Type: TEXT Description: Transcript Name from GENCODE
Column name: sample_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA sample barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A. One sample may have multiple sets of CN segmentations corresponding to multiple aliquots; use GROUP BY appropriately in queries
Column name: DbSNP_Val_Status Type: TEXT Description: DbSNP validation status is reported as a semicolon-separated list of statuses. The union of all rs-IDs is taken when there are multiple
Column name: cDNA_Change Type: TEXT Description: CDNA change. Examples: c.3236G>A,c.143_147delCTGCC, c.4417_4418insCAA
Column name: Sequencer Type: TEXT Description: Instrument used to produce primary sequence data
Column name: Normal_Seq_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype. Matched normal sequencing allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases (cleared in somatic MAF)
Column name: HGNC_Accession_Numbers Type: TEXT Description: HGNC Accession Numbers
Column name: Tumor_Validation_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Tumor genotyping (validation) for allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: Start_Position Type: NUMBER Description: Lowest numeric position of the reported variant on the genomic reference sequence. Mutation start coordinate
Column name: SwissProt_Entry_Id Type: TEXT Description: SwissProt Entry ID
Column name: Secondary_Variant_Classification Type: TEXT Description: Secondary Variant Classification
Column name: GENCODE_Transcript_Type Type: TEXT Description: Transcript Type from GENCODE, for more information: https://www.gencodegenes.org/pages/biotypes.html
Column name: Center Type: TEXT Description: One or more genome sequencing center reporting the variant
Column name: UniProt_AApos Type: NUMBER Description: UniProt AA position
Column name: Tumor_Validation_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Secondary data from orthogonal technology. Tumor genotyping (validation) for allele 2
Column name: SwissProt_Acc_Id Type: TEXT Description: SwissProt Accesssion ID
Column name: HGNC_Ensembl_ID_Supplied_By_Ensembl Type: TEXT Description: Ensembl ID
Column name: DrugBank Type: TEXT Description: Associated Drug Bank Names and IDs
Column name: aliquot_barcode_normal Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the normal control, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: GO_Molecular_Function Type: TEXT Description: GO Molecular Function, for more information: http://geneontology.org/docs/ontology-documentation/
Column name: project_short_name Type: TEXT Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; eg. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: Chromosome Type: TEXT Description: Chromosome, possible values: chr1-22, and chrX
Column name: End_Position Type: NUMBER Description: End position, in 1-based integer coordinates
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 2. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: Refseq_Prot_Id Type: TEXT Description: RefSeq Protein ID e.g. NP_000134.2
Column name: GC_Content Type: FLOAT Description: Percent GC content
Column name: HGNC_UCSC_ID_Supplied_By_UCSC Type: TEXT Description: UCSC ID
Column name: GENCODE_Transcript_Status Type: TEXT Description: Transcript Status from GENCODE
Column name: GO_Biological_Process Type: TEXT Description: GO Biological Process, for more information: http://geneontology.org/docs/ontology-documentation/
Column name: Mutation_Status Type: TEXT Description: An assessment of the mutation as somatic, germline, LOH, post transcriptional modification, unknown, or none. The values allowed in this field are constrained by the value in the Validation_Status field
Column name: case_barcode Type: TEXT Description: Original TCGA case barcode, eg TCGA-12-1089  --  note that each case typically has a primary-tumor sample and a matched-normal (blood or adjacent tissue) sample; please refer to the TCGA Biospecimen table for more details
Column name: HGNC_OMIM_ID_Supplied_By_NCBI Type: TEXT Description: OMIM ID
Column name: Transcript_Strand Type: TEXT Description: DNA strand (1 or -1) on which the transcript/feature lies
Column name: Transcript_Exon Type: NUMBER Description: Transcript Exon
Column name: HGNC_Locus_Type Type: TEXT Description: HGNC Locus Type
Column name: Transcript_Position Type: TEXT Description: Transcript Position
Column name: HGNC_RefSeq_Supplied_By_NCBI Type: TEXT Description: RefSeq ID
Column name: HGNC_HGNC_ID Type: NUMBER Description: HGNC ID
Column name: aliquot_barcode_tumor Type: TEXT Description: TCGA aliquot barcode for the tumor, eg TCGA-12-1089-01A-01D-0517-01
Column name: Variant_Type Type: TEXT Description: Type of mutation. TNP (tri-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to DNP (di-nucleotide polymorphism) but for three consecutive nucleotides. ONP (oligo-nucleotide polymorphism) is analogous to TNP but for consecutive runs of four or more (SNP, DNP, TNP, ONP, INS, DEL, or Consolidated)
Column name: CCLE_ONCOMAP_Total_Mutations_In_Gene Type: NUMBER Description: Total number of mutations in genes in CCLE Oncomap data
Column name: Hugo_Symbol Type: TEXT Description: HUGO symbol for the gene (HUGO symbols are always in all caps). Unknown is used for regions that do not correspond to a gene
Column name: HGNC_CCDS_IDs Type: TEXT Description: HGNC CCDS IDs
Column name: Reference_Allele Type: TEXT Description: The plus strand reference allele at this position. Includes the deleted sequence for a deletion or - for an insertion
Column name: DNARepairGenes_Role Type: TEXT Description: DNA Repair Genes Role
Column name: NCBI_Build Type: TEXT Description: The reference genome used for the alignment (GRCh37)
Column name: Gene_Type Type: TEXT Description: Gene type. eg protein_coding, lincRNA, etc
Column name: Normal_Seq_Allele2 Type: TEXT Description: Matched normal sequencing allele 2
Column name: Genome_Change Type: TEXT Description: Location and Base Genome Change
Column name: Tumor_Seq_Allele1 Type: TEXT Description: Primary data genotype for tumor sequencing (discovery) allele 1. A - symbol for a deletion represents a variant. A - symbol for an insertion represents wild-type allele. Novel inserted sequence for insertion does not include flanking reference bases
Column name: Sequence_Source Type: TEXT Description: Molecular assay type used to produce the analytes used for sequencing. Allowed values are a subset of the SRA 1.5 library_strategy field values. This subset matches those used at CGHub
Column name: Annotation_Transcript Type: TEXT Description: Ensembl Annotation Transcript ID (e.g. ENST00000366560.3)
Column name: DbSNP_RS Type: TEXT Description: dbSNP reference SNP number, eg rs121913500 -- may be a comma-delimited list, or may be null
